cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ESP1 — Equilateral Small Polygons: First-Order Optimisation and Rigidity"
abstract: >-
  ESP1 is a computational tool for verifying sufficient conditions for strict local
  maximality of perimeter among equilateral small polygons. Based on realised diameter
  graphs, it combines exact algebra, validated interval arithmetic, positive active
  diameter multipliers and infinitesimal rigidity to establish local maximality modulo
  orientation-preserving Euclidean motions. A complementary Lean 4 formalisation is also
  provided. As principal applications, ESP1 rigorously verifies strict local maximality
  for the Bingane-Audet polygons A16, A32 and A64, and for the configurations Z32 and Z64
  reconstructed from their published descriptions. For n = 32, 64, the polygons Z_n have
  strictly larger perimeters than A_n, demonstrating the coexistence of distinct strict
  local maximisers with different perimeters. The software accompanies the article
  "First Order Geometry of Equilateral Small Polygons" by J. Ayala Hoffmann and
  T. Ayala Coppola.
type: software
notes: "Named Chiquipoli up to release 1.3.1 (Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23749398); renamed ESP1 on 2026-11-10."
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
